/* Haven: reaction pills (room timeline and Social both render through the same shared-components
   ReactionsRowButton) are a CSS Module there, so its own class names can't be targeted from a
   plain stylesheet like this one - only its custom *properties* cross that boundary cleanly
   (property values aren't module-scoped, only class/id selectors are). Same mechanism
   _EventTile.pcss already uses to pass its own highlight color into the same shared component
   tree - see that file's own comment. mx_MatrixChat_reactionPillSizeNormal is applied by
   LoggedInView.tsx from the Haven.reactionPillSize setting, mirroring how
   mx_MatrixChat_useCompactLayout already works for the layout setting. */
.mx_MatrixChat_reactionPillSizeNormal {
    /* Stock Element's own original values, before Haven's own bump to heading-md/22px/heading-sm -
       see ReactionsRowButton.module.css's own doc on exactly what changed and why. */
    --haven-reaction-pill-line-height: var(--cpd-font-size-heading-sm);
    --haven-reaction-pill-image-size: 16px;
    --haven-reaction-pill-emoji-font-size: var(--cpd-font-size-body-md);
}
